>> title: Kheer
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: rice, milk, cardamom, saffron, indian, stovetop
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 15 min
>> step.2: simmer 45 min until reduced
>> step.4: stir in the sugar
>> step.5: stir in the saffron and nuts
>> step.6: chill 2 hr, or serve warm

Toast @basmati rice{1/3%cup}(65 g, rinsed and drained), @ghee{1%tsp}(5 g) in a #heavy pot{} for ~{2%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)rice{} in @whole milk{6%cup}(1.4 L), stirring often, until it reduces by a third.

Steep @saffron{1/4%tsp}(a large pinch) in @warm milk{2%Tbs}(30 mL).

Stir @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g), @green cardamom{1/2%tsp}(seeds from 6 pods, crushed) into @&(~2)kheer{}.

Stir @&(~2)saffron milk{} into @&(~1)sweetened kheer{} with @slivered almonds{1/4%cup}(30 g), @pistachios{2%Tbs}(15 g, slivered), @golden raisins{2%Tbs}(20 g).

Chill @&(~1)kheer{} for ~{2%hr}, or serve it warm.
